From: Syrupdesu <122212359+Syrupdesu@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 23:10:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] winex11.drv: Don't wait forever for the pointer grab on focus
 change.

wait_grab_pointer() retries XGrabPointer() every 10ms until it succeeds.
That never happens when the grab is held by another thread of the same
process that is blocked in a synchronous SendMessage() to the thread
changing focus: the sender cannot release the grab before its message is
processed, and the receiver cannot process the message before the grab is
released.

Reproduced with Arknights: Endfield 1.6.3 (Steam AppID 4732690) on KWin
Wayland in desktop mode. Opening the in-game web view creates a Qt
WebEngine window and the main thread ends up in

  NtUserPeekMessage -> X11DRV_ProcessEvents -> X11DRV_ClientMessage ->
  set_focus -> wait_grab_pointer

while another thread of the same process is stuck in
send_inter_thread_message -> wait_message_reply. Because the pointer grab
is global, the rest of the desktop stops receiving pointer input as well,
which makes the Steam client look frozen too.

Stop waiting after one second so that the pending message can be
processed and the grab released. The original purpose of the wait,
delaying WM_ACTIVATE while the window manager is still moving or resizing
the window, is preserved for grabs shorter than that.
---
diff --git a/dlls/winex11.drv/event.c b/dlls/winex11.drv/event.c
--- a/dlls/winex11.drv/event.c
+++ b/dlls/winex11.drv/event.c
@@ -324,6 +324,7 @@ static Bool filter_event( Display *display, XEvent *event, char *arg )
 static void wait_grab_pointer( Display *display )
 {
     RECT rect;
+    unsigned int retries = 0;
 
     /* unnecessary on gamescope, windows cannot be moved with the mouse */
     if (X11DRV_HasWindowManager( "steamcompmgr" )) return;
@@ -336,6 +337,17 @@ static void wait_grab_pointer( Display *display )
                          None, None, CurrentTime ) != GrabSuccess)
     {
         LARGE_INTEGER timeout = {.QuadPart = -10 * (ULONGLONG)10000};
+
+        /* The grab can be held by another thread of this process which is
+         * waiting for us to process a sent message, in which case it will
+         * never be released. Stop waiting after a while so that the message
+         * can be processed. */
+        if (++retries >= 100)
+        {
+            WARN( "giving up waiting for pointer grab\n" );
+            break;
+        }
+
         NtDelayExecution( FALSE, &timeout );
     }
 
